.TH TRIER-BRIDGE-TRAY 1 "2026-09-21" "trier-bridge 0.1.0~dev0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trier-bridge-tray \- the Trier Bridge tray icon "T"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trier-bridge-tray
.RI [ \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a small "T" in the top bar with a menu that opens Trier Bridge, opens its
Integrations page, or turns the tray icon off. It is a StatusNotifierItem and is
displayed by the desktop's AppIndicator support (enabled by default on Ubuntu).
.PP
It runs only if the user turned the "Tray icon T at login" integration on; then
a per-user autostart entry starts it at login. Turning the integration off, from
the menu or from the Integrations page, closes the icon and deletes that entry.
If no StatusNotifier host is present it exits after two minutes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Also write the log to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/org.triertech.TrierBridge.Tray.desktop
the autostart entry written by the integration
.TP
.I ~/.config/trier-bridge/integrations.json
the integration ledger it updates when turned off from its menu
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trier-bridge (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Doug Trier
